IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory): the dictionary entries that an in-scope provision uses,
-- and every entry about time, commencement, laws, instruments and the Territory.
--
-- Part 1 of the dictionary defines terms used in all Acts and statutory instruments (s 144).
-- Part 2 defines terms used in this Act only (s 2, Note 3).
-- One constant for each entry, written by a script that reads the text file.
-- The other entries of the dictionary are not in this module: no in-scope provision uses them.
-- The text is the unofficial plain-text rendering deposited with this encoding, not the authorised republication.

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT): dictionary`

-- src:2808 | Act—see the following sections:
-- src:2809 | (a) section 7 (Meaning of Act generally);
-- src:2810 | (b) section 17 (References to Acts include references to former Cwlth enactments etc).
-- src:2811 | Note See also s 102 (References to laws include references to laws as in force from time to time) and s 104 (References to laws include references to instruments under laws).
@ref dictionary pt 1, Act (src:2808-2811)
GIVETH A `Definition`
`dictionary pt 1: Act` MEANS
    `Definition` WITH
        `term` IS "Act"
        `how it is defined` IS `a signpost definition`
        `applies to` IS "all Acts and statutory instruments (dictionary, part 1)"
        `meaning as printed` IS "Act—see the following sections:"
        `further lines as printed` IS LIST ("(a) section 7 (Meaning of Act generally);"), ("(b) section 17 (References to Acts include references to former Cwlth enactments etc).")

