-- The in-scope dictionary entry for the term, as the dictionary prints the term (with its ", for ..." qualification if it has one).
-- NOTHING if the term has no in-scope entry.
GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Definition`
`dictionary: the in-scope entry for the term` MEANS `the dictionary entry found for` term `the in-scope entries of the dictionary`

GIVEN term IS A STRING, entries IS A LIST OF `Definition`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Definition`
`the dictionary entry found for` MEANS
    CONSIDER entries
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   first's `term` EQUALS term
        THEN JUST first
        ELSE `the dictionary entry found for` term rest
